<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">charm</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Charm</ansi> spell reaches into a creature's mind and bends its will to
yours, turning it into a loyal companion. The creature will follow you
and fight at your side until the hold on its mind fades.

Success is determined by an opposed roll — your charisma and
manifestation skill against the creature's willpower and mental
fortitude. Creatures already in combat are harder to charm, as their
minds are focused on survival rather than open to influence.

Your hold gradually loosens over time. When the charm finally breaks,
the creature reverts to its natural state and may turn hostile. The
stronger your charisma and the higher your manifestation skill, the
longer the charm endures.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast charm</ansi>             Attempts to charm your current combat target.
  <ansi fg="command">cast charm [target]</ansi>    Targets a specific creature by name.

<ansi fg="yellow">Casting:     </ansi> Long channel — requires deep concentration
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> Single creature
<ansi fg="yellow">Defense:     </ansi> Mental (opposed by target's willpower)
<ansi fg="yellow">Duration:    </ansi> Scales with charisma and manifestation skill
<ansi fg="yellow">Conv. Cost:  </ansi> Very high — drains most of your conviction
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> Manifestation

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - Charm cannot be used on other players.
  - Merchants, powerful named creatures, and certain others are
    immune — their minds are beyond your reach.
  - Creatures already in combat resist more strongly. Engaging a
    target before casting gives it an edge in the mental contest.
  - You may only have a limited number of companions at once.
    Release one with <ansi fg="command">dismiss</ansi> before charming another.
  - If the charm breaks while the creature is near you, expect it
    to become hostile immediately.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help manifestation</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help companion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help dismiss</ansi>
